caseStudy:
  problem: "Video sells products, but an autoplay clip is easy to scroll past and a large video file slows the page down, especially on phones."
  built: "A product page where an eight-second studio film is cut into WebP frames and painted to a canvas as you scroll, so the visitor controls the film. Phones get a smaller, cropped sequence of 72 frames that loads after the page is ready, coarse frames first. A pinned gallery, a numbers section and a specification table carry the detail, and with reduced motion switched on the film becomes a calm still and the page reads top to bottom."
